good evening members and officers of the  council and members of the press and  public i welcome you to this meeting of  the council thursday 7th february 2019  if i can just run through the  housekeeping quickly if the fire alarm  is activated please vacate the offices  via the stairs either through the  security doors to my right or opposite  the lifts in the foyer  please do not use the lifts  please assemble in holy square on the  green officers will assist you and  advise when it is deemed safe to return  to the chamber  i can confirm the proceedings of this  meeting will be recorded and  subsequently  broadcast on the internet  i would advise that if filming takes  place anyone in attendance in the public  areas may have their image captured i  urge anyone filming proceedings to avoid  filming members of the public  particularly if they are  our children present  i won't ask the next question which is  does anyone intend to film the meeting  i have been to spec savers  any member of the public who objects to  the possibility of being filmed may wish  to take this opportunity to leave the  meeting any filming or recording will  not be permitted for any item of  business where exempt or confidential  information  is considered following the exclusion of  the press and public from the meeting  can i ask everyone present to please  ensure that their mobile phones are  turned to silent and that they are not  used to make or receive phone calls in  the chamber whilst the meeting is in  progress  we can move on to the agenda and agenda  item one is apologies for absence  i've so far received apologies from  councillors dixon falcon grove larkins  shank schtummerschmerzing  town and hillman and our pots  are there any other apologies council  fairgrounds  thank you  okay  can i announce before we get to  the next agenda item  that a agenda item  six budget  2019-20 report has been withdrawn from  this evening's meeting  i would ask the leader to explain the  circumstances council bayford yeah thank  you chairman um i mean members will be  aware that um i've said all along for a  long time that  we couldn't carry on uh with the  never-ending saga of the port of  ramsgate and we had to reach a point  where we either had an operator and  therefore income to meet the cost or we  had to actually make the very  uncomfortable decision to actually close  sections of the port and make serious  cost savings  but today i had a conversation with  chris grayling secretary of state  department of transport  the dft is continuing commercial  discussions with seabourn and other  potential operators recognising the  importance of ramsgate port in terms of  brexit resilience the department for  transport is very keen to keep the  option of ramsgate alive and in the  light of this i'll ask the chairman to  withdraw the item tonight for it to come  back at the soonest opportunity when  those discussions have been concluded  thank you  can the leader or yourself tell us when  the last date for the actual  verification of the budget can take  place  council of athens sorry i'm told legally  the 11th of march we have to allow  sufficient time to get the council tax  decision for it to be implemented okay  thank you we'll continue with the  agenda items and agenda item two is  minutes of the extraordinary meeting  held on the 27th of november 2018  i move that the minutes of the  extraordinary meeting of the council  held on the 27th of november be approved  and signed as a correct record  with the vice chairman please second  second lecture  do members agree  thank you  agenda item three minutes of the meeting  held on the 6th of december 2018  i move that the minutes of the meeting  of the council held on the 6th of  december 2018  be approved and signed as a correct  record  once again with the vice chairman plea  second second here do members agree  thank you  general item 4 announcements  it is with regret that i have to  announce that former councillor simon  morse has recently passed away mr morris  was a conservative councillor from 2007  to 2015 and a cabinet member for  environmental services  sadly  it is also with regret that i have to  announce that former councillor ronald  hatton has also recently passed away mr  hutton was a conservative councillor  from  1991 to 1994.  i'm sure the council will join me in  expressing sympathy to both mr moors and  mr hutton's family  could all members please stand for a  minute silence as a mark of respect for  the late mr moors and mr hutton  thank you  does any member wish to say a few words  councillor hayden  thank you very much german  i knew and worked with um both gentlemen  but mainly with ron hutton he joined the  council  in 91 as i did  um people used to get mixed up with he  and i  because of our names hutton and hayden  was too close  the only difference was that uh ron  hotten was a multi-millionaire  and i was a vagrant from the poor side  of ramsgate  the  the situation with ron is that he wasn't  political  he just wanted to see what he could do  for the people of thanet  and  he became deputy leader of this council  and  obviously really enjoyed himself  he used to disrupt  the  agenda  in the planning  committee especially when i was chairman  of that  meeting  and he  he was a very  good nice gentleman and his family were  very very good  as for um  the other i don't know didn't know very  much about him perhaps counselor bayford  knew more where to them than i did but  simon moore was a  a different character to ron hutton  um  he was he was a very hard working  counselor  and  he  was on the cabinet  and uh did some very good work  and uh we shall mess both of these  gentlemen thank you very much jim  thank you councillor hayden council  bayford  yes thank you chairman i suppose it's  the reversal he said i mean i didn't  really know ron hubbard very well um i  mean he was here for a term became  deputy leader um and unfortunately for  him he wasn't one of the three that  survived of the 34 of us that had been  here in 95  and i think that was a great loss to  this council because uh you know was set  i mean he was passionate about the area  and uh only wanted to see you know good  happen so it's a shame that he wasn't  here for longer  um there's simon moore yes he was  colleague for eight years um both a  backbencher and a cabinet member  he was highly intelligent very  articulate when he spoke he was always  worth listening to  he was a passionate advocate for  westgate  and i suppose the only consolation that  you can take from this that he died  doing something that he really loved  flying  thank you council bayford  thank you very much um chairman um yes i  knew ron hutton as well i'm afraid i  might have been a bit of a thorn in his  side prior to the 95 elections when i  was campaigning with labour members for  pensioners bus passes and lavatories and  i'm not going to go into the gory  details but i did come one night to a  meeting and wave a red bucket around and  embarrassed for mr hutton councillor  hutton i said is this what we're reduced  to but of course i've matured since then  i wouldn't do such a thing now  [Laughter]  i really i didn't know that ron had died  and obviously our group would be very  sorry to hear that for his anybody's  family and so  but um i knew simon much more so and  simon was a formidable and political  opponent i did write to the leader and  to sir roger gail because whatever  arouse we have in here we often work  closely together outside of here and  many times both when he was in a cabinet  position or later when i was a deputy  leader and even a leader he would  contact me about issues in westgate i  know that privately and behind the  scenes he did a lot of work with  homeless people in adrian square  he would be the first to pick up a phone  to me to say  we found particularly young women we  found i'm sleeping rough and he and i  know from an officer here at the time  that he would bring down food and  blankets and be generous  as i said he was a formidable political  opponent he was an intelligent person  it's a very sad loss for your party and  for his family and i think as i say when  we have our rows in here it's what we do  outside of here that matters and we did  get the pensioners bus passes in the end  thank you  thank you council johnson  right we move on to agenda item seven  treasury management strategy statement  and annual investment strategy mid-year  review report 2018-2019  i call upon councillor gregory  thank you chairman um this mid-year um  treasury management review to report to  council is a requirement of the  chartered institute of public finance  accountancy and provides details of the  council's treasury performance to the  end of september 2018.  the treasury management strategy  statement for 2018-19 which includes the  annual investment strategy was approved  by council on the 8th of february 2018.  there are no policy changes to the  treasury management strategy statement  and the annual investment strategy that  was previously approved  the council held 47.49 million in  investment at mid-year up from 40.88 at  the 31st 80 million at the 31st of march  investment yield was 0.6 against the  seven day local interbank bid benchmark  of 0.44  the return on investment was budgeted at  62 000 but was well above budget at 136  000 by mid year  original estimate for the capital  financing requirements was 57.17 million  and at mid-year it was held down to 30.7  million by utilizing 25.4 million of  cash flow funds in lieu of borrowing  no debt rescheduling took place due to  the prevailing interest rate structure  the debt interest budget was set at 1.5  million but is revised down to an  estimated 1.2 million by year end  finally the ratio of financing costs to  revenue stream is down on both the  non-hra and the hra budgets  non-hra is down from 10.5 percent of  revenue stream to 8.6  and hra is down from 7.6 of revenue  stream to 6  this mid-year report shows good  performance in all areas and i propose  that council approves the report and the  treasury indicators shown  thank you councillor gregory is their  seconder  council bayford  members i have an apology to make i've  got a little bit carried away myself and  i've skipped agenda item five this  wasn't a deliberate mistake  so agenda item five is declarations of  interest are there any declarations of  interest counselor campbell i think the  collective uh  declaration of interest in the members  allowance scheme  and agenda item  we've we've already covered that sorry  yes there is already a general  dispensation in place for members of  ourselves  thank you any other declarations of  interest  once again apologies members  do we wish to debate agenda item seven  so eloquently um presented by councillor  gregory  councillor piper  thank you chairman i'm just gonna be a  tiny little bit cheeky if you'll allow  it  this forms part of  the amount of work that mr willis and  his team have done  in the last 12 months to try and work  magic  a bit like the hebrews making bricks  without straw they've done an  extraordinary difficult job  and i believe  whether we agree fully with exactly what  the outcome has has become they still  deserve the thanks of members in this  chamber for the work that they have put  in to try as i say and work  magic it's a shame and this is where i'm  being a bit cheeky and perhaps some  clearance could be given clear guidance  could be given to us  uh whether the decision to pull it was  ours or whether it was a government  decision interfering with democratic  process in this place because whatever's  happened they have not allowed elected  members in this place to do their jobs  and do them properly for the benefit of  the people of senec so thank you for  letting me express my disappointment but  also my thanks to mr willis and his team  cheeky as ever counselor piper but as  you know i tend to be quite generous but  uh  thank you um do members agree  with councillor gregory  thank you  gender item eight members allowance  scheme 2019-20  i move that the recommendation has set  out in the report be adopted with the  vice chairman please second  i second that yeah  sorry another one  thank you  do members agree oh council bayford  thank you chairman i'd like to be as  cheeky as councillor piper and answer  his question and say that it was my  request to you to postpone the budget  tonight because i thought it was the  best thing we should do it's not denying  uh democratic rights at the budget in  fact it's creating the situation will be  better informed to create the right  budget  thank you council bayford for that uh  explanation  and defense of my position  uh we're on members allowance scheme do  members agree  thank you  that concludes the business for the  meeting this evening of the council

